01\u7684\u8fb9\u754c\u3002\u8fd9\u6b21\u5bf9\u8c08\uff0c\u6211\u4eec\u4ece\u4e00\u90e8\u90e8\u4f5c\u54c1\u804a\u8d77\uff0c\u843d\u5230\u4e00\u4e2a\u5e76\u4e0d\u8f7b\u677e\u7684\u95ee\u9898\u4e0a\uff1a\u5982\u679c\u6709\u4e00\u5929\u7845\u57fa\u667a\u80fd\u771f\u7684\u5230\u6765\uff0c\u78b3\u57fa\u7684\u6211\u4eec\u8be5\u5982\u4f55\u81ea\u5904\u3002<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.66309\/2nj6aa03","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,3]],"date-time":"2026-10-03T09:36:29Z","timestamp":1791020189000},"page":"e0011","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["\u5f53\u5b85\u5708\u9047\u4e0a\u7b2c\u4e00\u6027\u539f\u7406\uff1a\u4e00\u4f4d\u8ba1\u7b97\u751f\u7269\u5b66\u8005\u773c\u4e2d\u7684 ACG\u3001\u4eba\u5de5\u667a\u80fd\u4e0e\u7845\u57fa\u672a\u6765"],"prefix":"10.66309","volume":"1","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0007-3615-5724","authenticated-orcid":true,"family":"Zhaoshuo","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/03angcq70","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"University of Birmingham"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jiarui","family":"Zhou","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"55911","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,3]]},"container-title":["ACGN Nexus"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/journal.scihorizon.org\/index.php\/ACGN\/article\/download\/32\/22","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/journal.scihorizon.org\/index.php\/ACGN\/article\/download\/32\/22","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,3]],"date-time":"2026-10-03T09:36:30Z","timestamp":1791020190000},"score":0.0,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/journal.scihorizon.org\/index.php\/ACGN\/article\/view\/32"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,3]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,12,31]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.66309\/2nj6aa03","ISSN":["3142-8452"],"issn-type":[{"value":"3142-8452","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,3]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,21]],"date-time":"2026-09-21T08:06:29Z","timestamp":1789977989331,"version":"4.0.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"SciHorizon Global LLC","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,21]],"date-time":"2026-09-21T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1789948800000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["ACGN Nex."],"abstract":"<jats:p>The Seishun Buta Yaro series employs the supernatural concept of \u201cAdolescence Syndrome\u201d as its central narrative device, transforming the psychological conflicts that adolescents struggle to articulate into visible and tangible phenomena. Drawing primarily on psychosocial developmental theory, object relations theory, and symbolic interactionism, this paper examines the psychological issues of self-identity, interpersonal relationships, traumatic experiences, and social evaluation reflected in different manifestations of \u201cAdolescence Syndrome.\u201d Rather than representing a disease in the medical sense, \u201cAdolescence Syndrome\u201d functions as a literary mechanism for externalizing psychological experiences: it projects internal conflicts that are difficult for individuals to integrate into the external world, giving concrete and perceptible form to such internal relationships as \u201cseeing-being seen,\u201d \u201cself-other,\u201d \u201creal self-ideal self,\u201d and \u201cpast-future.\u201d Likewise, \u201ccompletion\u201d does not signify the elimination of personal flaws, the erasure of suffering, or the attainment of a flawless self; instead, it represents the reintegration of those aspects of the self that have been denied, fragmented, or not yet understood into a complete and continuous life narrative. From this perspective, adolescence should not be regarded as a \u201cproblematic period\u201d that must be rapidly overcome, but rather as a crucial stage of personality development and self-reconstruction. Instead of demanding that adolescents become so-called \u201cperfect adults\u201d as quickly as possible, it is more important to provide them with stable and reliable relationships, sufficient space for self-expression, and necessary professional support, enabling them, through being understood and accepted, to gradually develop the capacities to understand themselves, take responsibility for their choices, establish personal boundaries, and build healthy relationships with others.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.66309\/66363s17","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,21]],"date-time":"2026-09-21T07:59:19Z","timestamp":1789977559000},"page":"e0010","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["&lt;b&gt;\u5fc3\u7075\u7684\u5177\u8c61\u5316\uff1a\u5fc3\u7406\u5b66\u89c6\u89d2\u4e0b\u300a\u9752\u6625\u732a\u5934\u5c11\u5e74\u300b\u4e2d\u7684\u81ea\u6211\u5f62\u6210\u4e0e\u201c\u8865\u5b8c\u201d&lt;\/b&gt;"],"prefix":"10.66309","volume":"1","author":[{"family":"Darren","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/013xs5b60","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"\u9996\u90fd\u533b\u79d1\u5927\u5b66"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"55911","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,21]]},"container-title":["ACGN Nexus"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/journal.scihorizon.org\/index.php\/ACGN\/article\/download\/30\/21","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/journal.scihorizon.org\/index.php\/ACGN\/article\/download\/30\/21","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","int